│            │                         │ │ Forget? RAM leak ──────> Crash!    │
│            ▼                         │ │            │                       │
│ Java's Design:                       │ │            ▼                       │
│   "Group data & behavior together!"  │ │ JVM Solution (The Bodyguard):      │
│            │                         │ │ ┌──────────────────────────────┐   |  
│            ▼                         │ │ │ Stack  : Static vars (Fast)  │   |
│   Class  = Blueprint (Human-friendly │ │ │ Heap   : 'new Object()' RAM  │   |
│   Object = Dynamic Copy (Instance)   │ │ │ Garbage: Auto-deletes RAM!   │   |
│            │                         │ │ └──────────────────────────────┘   |
│            ▼                         │ │                                    │
│ Makes code easier for humans.        │ │                                    │
│ (CPU/RAM just see 1s and 0s)         │ │                                    │
└──────────────────────────────────────┘ └───────────────────────────────────-┘
┌─ SUMMARY ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  1. Must 'new Object()': Build the house before opening the door.           │
│  2. Dynamic: # of objects decided at runtime based on user input.           │
│  3. RAM survives: JVM auto-alloc & deletes via Garbage Collector.           │
│  => JVM wasn't the reason for objects; it was the bodyguard making them     │
│     safe!                                                                   │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

